# Scratch-file patterns are ANCHORED with a leading slash. A pattern with no
# slash matches at ANY depth: a bare junit.xml in a product .gitignore silently
# excluded a required committed fixture in P060 of this mission, and a cold
# clone then failed with 17 failures and 9 errors while every local check
# passed. validation/validate_tree_hygiene.py checks both directions with an
# explicit pattern matcher over this file and the repository root's, because
# this product's build agent is forbidden to run any git command;
# `git check-ignore -v` is the authority and belongs to the release gate.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
/build/
/dist/
/.venv/
/venv/
/.pytest_cache/
/.hypothesis/
/.ruff_cache/
/.coverage
/htmlcov/
/junit.xml
/.config/
# This product ships NO serialised model. The registry declares
# ai_enabled: false and there is no learned component to serialise; these
# patterns exist so that one cannot be added without the exclusion being
# noticed.
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.joblib
# The MEASURED hardware traces are NOT ignored. data/traces/ is this product's
# evidence and every file in it must reach a cold clone, including the raw
# per-cell arrays. They are listed as negations so that a future broad pattern
# cannot swallow them silently.
!/data/traces/
!/data/traces/*.csv
!/data/traces/meta.json
!/data/traces/raw/
!/data/traces/raw/*.npy
# The campaign's own log is evidence: it carries the eleven calibration medians
# and the per-cell completion lines in the order they happened, and
# validation/validate_independent_bound.py parses its per-cell median totals as
# a data path independent of the CSVs. The MISSION repository's root .gitignore
# has a bare `*.log`, which matches at any depth and WOULD silently exclude it;
# this negation, being in a deeper .gitignore, takes precedence for that file.
!/data/traces/campaign.log
